    "# 1 · GRB afterglow model\n",
    "\n",
    "Builds the emission model that `3_upper_limits` injects: **one fixed jet** from the Nava (2020) /\n",
    "Abe et al. (2026) recipe, every input at its population median (`BENCHMARK`), seen off-axis with\n",
    "the element integral of Abe et al. Sec. 3.4. It is tabulated on a 1° grid in $\\theta_v$ and saved to\n",
    "`data/models/grb_afterglow_phenomenological/benchmark/`. Run once.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why one fixed jet is enough.** Every realisation is rescaled to the trial luminosity $L_k$ over the\n",
    "GTIs, so anything that only multiplies $L$ drops out of the limit: the $L_X$ and $L_\\mathrm{TeV}/L_X$\n",
    "scatters and the amplitude part of $E_{\\gamma,\\mathrm{iso}}$. Only inputs that change the *shape*\n",
    "reach it: $\\theta_\\mathrm{core}$, $\\Gamma_\\mathrm{core}$, $\\beta_2$, the photon index and the time\n",
    "scale. §5 measures them.\n",
    "\n",
    "Code: [`gwuls/grb_phenomenological.py`](../gwuls/grb_phenomenological.py). Physics:\n",
    "[`docs/emission_model.md`](../docs/emission_model.md).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contents.** 1 The benchmark jet · 2 The off-axis element integral (+ checks) · 3 The benchmark at\n",
    "every angle · 4 Cross-check against the catO5 files · 5 Population scatter · 6 Save · 7 Caveats"
   ]
  },
