    "## 1. The benchmark jet\n",
    "\n",
    "Every input is the median of its population distribution in Nava (2020) and Abe et al. (2026).\n",
    "The last column says whether the input can reach an upper limit on $L_k$ at all.\n",
    "\n",
    "| input | description | benchmark | population | reaches the $L_k$ limit? |\n",
    "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n",
    "| $E_{\\gamma,\\mathrm{iso}}$ | Isotropic-equivalent prompt gamma-ray energy | $2.0\\times10^{50}$ erg | $E_\\mathrm{peak}$ broken power law, then Amati (Ghirlanda et al. 2016) | only through the time scale, $t\\propto E^{1/3}$ |\n",
    "| $\\theta_\\mathrm{core}$ | Half-opening angle of the jet core | 14.1° | lognormal, $\\log_{10}$ mean 1.15, σ 0.2 dex (Fong et al. 2015) | yes |\n",
    "| $\\Gamma_\\mathrm{core}$ | Initial bulk Lorentz factor of the jet core | 200 | lognormal, $\\log_{10}$ mean 2.3, σ 0.2 dex | yes, near the axis |\n",
    "| $\\beta_1$ (rise) | Temporal power-law index of the light-curve rise before the peak | 2 | normal, σ 0.05 | negligibly |\n",
    "| $\\beta_2$ (decay) | Temporal power-law index of the light-curve decay after the peak | −1.45 | normal, σ 0.48 (22 short GRBs) | yes |\n",
    "| photon index $p$ | Spectral index of the photon spectrum, $dN/dE \\propto E^{-p}$ | 2.2 | normal, σ 0.1 | yes |\n",
    "| $L_\\mathrm{TeV,11h}$ | Intrinsic 0.3–1 TeV luminosity at $t'=11$ h (brightness anchor) | mean relations: $L_X$ from Berger (2014), $L_\\mathrm{TeV}/L_X=1$ | 0.5 dex and 0.3 dex lognormal scatter | no, amplitude only |\n",
    "| $n$, $\\eta_\\gamma$ | Circumburst number density and prompt radiative efficiency | 0.1 cm⁻³, 0.2 | fixed in both sources | — |\n",
    "\n",
    "The median $E_{\\gamma,\\mathrm{iso}}$ depends on the lower cut of the $E_\\mathrm{peak}$ distribution\n",
    "(`EPEAK_MIN_KEV`). It is recomputed below, with the 16th/84th percentiles that\n",
    "`one_sigma_variants` uses."
   ]
