    "## 5. Population scatter\n",
    "\n",
    "The benchmark is a single jet. Adding random noise to the flux is not a way to include the\n",
    "population: multiplicative noise drops out under the $L_k$ normalisation, and noise on the shape\n",
    "means nothing unless it comes from the recipe's own distributions. Two valid options:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Nominal: the benchmark** (what `3_upper_limits` uses). The limit reads \"for the population's\n",
    "   median short GRB\".\n",
    "2. **Systematic band: one-sigma variants.** `one_sigma_variants(B)` moves one shape input at a time to\n",
    "   its 16th or 84th percentile. Rerunning the limit on the variant caches gives the band.\n",
    "\n",
    "(A third, a fixed bank of population draws marginalised per realisation, is possible with\n",
    "`draw_jet_params` but not implemented in the pipeline.)\n",
    "\n",
    "Which inputs matter? Each variant is compared with the benchmark in a reference window, a\n",
    "placeholder for the real GTIs, by two numbers:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **the log-slope in the window**: the shape, which is what survives the $L_k$ normalisation when the\n",
    "  exposure changes across the GTIs. With uniform exposure even this drops out, and the photon index\n",
    "  is the only input left;\n",
    "- **the change in fluence**: relevant only for a limit on the model's own normalisation."
   ]
