    "## 7. Caveats\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Smoothed on-axis peak.** The arrival-time spread across the beaming cone (§2.1) lowers the rise\n",
    "  (about 4×) and rounds the peak; the decay matches the recipe exactly. Follow-ups starting after\n",
    "  about a minute only see the decay.\n",
    "- **Element normalisation** $d\\Omega/\\Omega_\\mathrm{beam}(\\Gamma)$ is the standard point-source\n",
    "  choice; Lamb & Kobayashi's exact convention is not given. It matters most for late, mildly\n",
    "  relativistic material, where the 77.8° catO5 file disagrees in amplitude (§4).\n",
    "- **Simple dynamics:** Blandford–McKee deceleration, no lateral spreading, no non-relativistic\n",
    "  transition (Γ floored at 1), no counter-jet; truncated at $\\theta_\\mathrm{max}$ ($\\Gamma_0=5$).\n",
    "  These matter far off-axis at $t'\\gtrsim10^6$ s.\n",
    "- **Constant photon index** in time and angle, as in the recipe and the catO5 files.\n",
    "- **Readings of the sources:** the Eq. 1 width convention of `jet_structure`, the $t_\\mathrm{dec}$\n",
    "  prefactor $R_\\mathrm{dec}/(2c\\Gamma_0^2)$, and \"11 h\" as a rest-frame time.\n",
    "- **§5's window is a placeholder.** Redo the ranking with the real GTIs before quoting a band."
   ]
  }
